mode: "100644"
text: "# voice.md Template\n\nThe output of this skill. It must be **operational** — rules a writer or another skill can\nfollow — not a personality essay. Every rule should trace back to a sample. Keep it tight;\ndownstream skills read it on every task.\n\nCopy everything below the line into `voice.md` and fill it in.\n\n---\n\n```markdown\n# Voice — {Person or Brand Name}\n<!-- version: 1.0 · updated: {date} · confidence: {high | medium | low} · based on: {n} samples ({types}) -->\n\n## Voice fingerprint (the 5–7 signatures)\nThe few things that, done right, make writing recognizably theirs. Each must be reproducible.\n1. {e.g., Opens with a one-line provocation, then a blank line.}\n2. {e.g., Short declaratives (6–12 words), broken by one long sentence per paragraph.}\n3. {e.g., Self-deprecating dry humor; never at the customer's expense.}\n4. {e.g., Builds by contrast — \"everyone does X; do Y instead.\"}\n5. {e.g., Em-dashes for rhythm; never semicolons.}\n6. {e.g., Lands on a question or a short reframe, not a CTA.}\n\n## Never (the hard guardrails)\nThe negative space. Downstream skills must respect these.\n- Never {e.g., uses exclamation marks}.\n- Never {e.g., opens with \"I'm thrilled/excited to announce\"}.\n- Never {e.g., more than one emoji per post}.\n- Never {e.g., uses \"leverage,\" \"solution,\" \"utilize,\" \"game-changer\"}.\n- Never {e.g., dunks on a named competitor}.\n\n## Lexicon\n- **Register:** {plain/Anglo-Saxon ↔ formal/Latinate}\n- **Contractions:** {always / never / context}\n- **Signature words & phrases:** {the words they reach for; names for product/customer/category}\n- **Banned words:** {the wince list}\n- **Concreteness rule:** {e.g., one concrete example per post}\n\n## Syntax & rhythm\n- **Sentence pattern:** {e.g., short punches + one long; avg ~10 words}\n- **Openers:** {e.g., often \"And/But,\" or a question}\n- **Fragments:** {deliberate / no}\n- **Voice:** {active / passive}\n- **Punctuation rhythm:** {em-dashes, colons, ellipses, etc.}\n\n## Rhetoric\n- **Direct address:** {how much \"you\"}\n- **Devices they use:** {questions, contrast, repetition, analogy domain}\n- **Humor:** {type + what it never targets}\n- **The turn / landing:** {how they close a point}\n\n## Structure\n- **Opening move:** {hook style}\n- **Build:** {linear / layered / list / story}\n- **Close:** {default ending}\n- **Formatting & whitespace:** {paragraphing, lists, the scaffolding}\n\n## Stance\n- **Distance & posture:** {peer / mentor / expert / provocateur}\n- **Confidence:** {assertive / qualified}\n- **Emotional register:** {warm / cool / intense / playful}\n- **Self-disclosure:** {how much}\n- **For / against:** {what they champion and push against}\n\n## Tone map (how the voice flexes by context)\nVoice stays constant; tone shifts. Capture only the shifts that matter.\n- **LinkedIn / long-form:** {delta}\n- **TikTok / Reels:** {delta}\n- **Replies / community:** {delta}\n- **Bad news / crisis:** {delta — how the voice handles pressure}\n- **Celebration / wins:** {delta — without breaking the \"never\"s}\n\n## Do / don't rewrites\nShow the voice in action. 3–5 generic lines → the same thing in this voice.\n| Generic | In this voice |\n|---|---|\n| \"We're excited to announce our new feature.\" | {in-voice version} |\n| \"Here are 5 tips to grow your audience.\" | {in-voice version} |\n| \"Our product helps you save time.\" | {in-voice version} |\n\n## Calibration anchors (real snippets)\n2–4 short, real quotes from the samples that best capture the voice. Writers pattern-match\nagainst these.\n- \"{quote}\"\n- \"{quote}\"\n\n## Confidence & gaps\n- **Confidence:** {high / medium / low} based on {n} samples.\n- **Well-established:** {which layers are solid}\n- **Uncertain / needs more samples:** {which layers are thin}\n```\n\n---\n\n## How downstream skills should use this\n\nRead the **fingerprint**, the **never** list, and the **do/don't rewrites** on every task —\nthose three carry most of the voice. Use the **tone map** to adjust register for the platform.\nWhen unsure, match the **calibration anchors**. If a section is empty or low-confidence, write\nconservatively and flag it rather than inventing voice.\n"
